        <section
          class="gl-capabilities"
          id="capabilities"
        >
          <p
            class="section-label"
          >
            What I do
          </p>
          <p
            class="gl-capabilities__intro"
          >
            Systems, people, ideas, and possibilities — the boundaries between these blend best when connected by thoughtful communication. I build the technology, explore the questions, and create the conditions for meaningful exchange across all frontiers.
          </p>
          <div
            class="gl-capabilities__grid"
          >
            <article
              class="gl-capability-card"
            >
              <div
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="gl-capability-card__accent"
              />
              <h3>
                Technical Leadership
              </h3>
              <p>
                Understanding how things work and making them work better defines what I do: building software, shaping technical architecture, and leading initiatives that span systems, teams, and organizations, from enterprise platforms to emerging technologies.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article
              class="gl-capability-card"
            >
              <div
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="gl-capability-card__accent"
              />
              <h3>
                Product & Experimentation
              </h3>
              <p>
                I thrive in the messy space between "something isn't working" and "here's a better way." Experimentation, feedback, prototyping, and iteration lead us to better answers, clarifying which ideas deserve attention—and which are better left behind.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article
              class="gl-capability-card"
            >
              <div
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="gl-capability-card__accent"
              />
              <h3>
                Education & Communication
              </h3>
              <p>
                Making complicated things easier to understand has been the beating heart of my career. Whether I'm teaching, writing, publishing, designing workshops, or creating learning experiences for unique audiences, I care about clarity without flattening the complexity that makes an idea interesting.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article
              class="gl-capability-card"
            >
              <div
                aria-hidden="true"
                class="gl-capability-card__accent"
              />
              <h3>
                Organizational Enablement
              </h3>
              <p>
                Technology doesn't change organizations. People do. I help teams navigate the space between a new idea and the people who have to make it real—through mentorship, collaboration, communication, and thoughtful adoption.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <div
            class="gl-capabilities__cta"
          >
            <p>
              AI has become one of the most interesting places where these threads converge. What happens when powerful technology meets real people, real organizations, and imperfect systems? The answer depends on adopting it without losing sight of good judgment, trust, or the humans doing the work.
            </p>
            <a
              class="btn-secondary"
              href="/ai"
            >
              Read my AI philosophy
            </a>
          </div>
